# rpg/art/doll/clips/death.clip: the adult bodies' DEATH clips (FOLK-BODY; the P2b style slice). Format: rpg/art/doll/doll.h.
# (run fix i1, 2026-10-22) every frame naming hair=K also names braid=K (hair/adult/braid_hang has its own key channel)
# Fall (STYLE_P2 13; 0.10, 0.12, 0.12 s): recoil (the body jolts up, the arms flung up by the blow (arms `fling`, P2b
# production), the hurt face, the head snapped back), buckle (the knees
# give way, the head bowed), topple (the lying figure itself, 2 px up and 2 px toward where the body stood). Variant 0 falls
# west (head west), 1 east. Lying (SLICE-LYING-READ): the left view laid down by the doll's turn (by variant: 0 west, 1 east;
# one lying clip serves every facing) from painted lying keys (STYLE_P2 24): legs straight with the boots toes-up (`lie`),
# the near arm limp along the side with the hand on the ground (`lie`), the garment and the skirt draped to the ground
# (torso / hang `lie`), the hair pressed flat under the head (hairpose / hair `lie`: no lock below the back; a hood's drape the same, hatpose), the scarf's
# tail tucked (neck `lie`), the head forward 2 px so the skull's back rests on the ground with the back's; eyes closed. The
# body is 15 px tall. The sword lies on the ground in front, its grip under the hand (held `drop`, 4 px under the body's
# back): the sword's own clips (family sword, first, so they win) lift the pivot 4 px back onto the body's back, so the
# contact shadow and the corpse's baseline stay under the body.

body man
clip fall D variant 0 family sword
f armL=fling armR=fling legs=idle neck=rest sheath=rest torso=rest expr=hurt bob=-1 head=0,-1
f armL=idle armR=idle legs=buckle neck=rest sheath=rest torso=rest expr=hurt bob=3 head=0,1
f armL=lie armR=- hilt=- legs=lie neck=lie sheath=- torso=lie hang=lie hair=lie held=drop expr=closed hairpose=lie hatpose=lie head=-2,0 turn=west at=2,2 braid=lie
